<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jablonec nad Nisou</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Gablonz an der Neisse</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jablonec nad Nisou, in German Gablonz an der <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nysa">Neisse</a>, is a town in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czech-republic">Czech Republic</a>, famous since the 18th century for glass jewellery and costume ornaments. Its largely German population was expelled after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>, and many of the refugees resettled at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neugablonz">Neugablonz</a> near Kaufbeuren in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, where they rebuilt the industry.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jablonec-nad-nisou.jpg" alt="Jablonec nad Nisou" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Miloslav Rejha · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jablonec_nad_Nisou_2019-07_16.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
